<title>BULGARIA: Bulgaria sells 4.3 bln levs 3-mth discount T-bills.</title>
<headline>Bulgaria sells 4.3 bln levs 3-mth discount T-bills.</headline>
<dateline>SOFIA 1997-05-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bulgaria's Finance Ministry sold 4.286 billion levs of three-month discount T-bills, yielding 9.81 percent until maturity, central bank figures showed on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The issue was offered with no par value or minimum acceptable price set in advance for Monday's auction.</p>
<p>Details of the issue follow. Price in percent of par:</p>
<p> Issue number		 BG3032897004</p>
<p> Maturity		     three months</p>
<p> Auction date		 May 12</p>
<p> Issue date		   May 14</p>
<p> Maturity date		August 13</p>
<p> Bids received		58,732.5 million levs</p>
<p> Avg price of bids	  86.37 pct</p>
<p> Bids approved		4,285.7 million levs</p>
<p> Avg accepted price	 91.07 pct</p>
<p> Avg yield to maturity    9.81 pct</p>
<p>-- Sofia Newsroom, (++359-2) 91188</p>
</text>
